   "text": {
    "L1": "A phirki needs a push or pull to start moving.",
    "L2": "Moving air pushes its blades and makes them turn.",
    "L3": "When you hold it still in calm air, it does not spin.",
    "L4": "When you run, air rushes against the blades.",
    "L5": "The blades are bent, so the air push turns them round.",
    "L6": "Run faster and the air push is stronger, so the phirki spins faster.",
    "L7": "A moving thing does not stop because its push gets used up.",
    "L8": "Friction from the air and the ground slows moving things until they stop.",
    "L9": "With the same paper, longer wings catch more air and fall more slowly."
   },
